/target

# Cargo.lock is committed, which is a change from when this repository held only a library.
#
# It now also builds `pkwiz-solver`, published as release binaries whose SHA-256 consumers pin in
# their own source. A build that resolves dependencies differently from one run to the next
# produces a different digest for the same tag, which is exactly the thing those consumers are
# checking for. Committing the lockfile is what makes a rebuild of a tag reproduce its artifacts.
